LEUT BLOCKED (link#227) — 1 blocking dam(s) on LEUT's downstream flow path have not been modelled yet.

link computes accessibility by reading ALREADY-PERSISTED downstream barriers.
Running LEUT now would mark segments accessible that are in fact dammed off, and exit 0.

  persist schema : fresh_default
  unmodelled blocking dams downstream of LEUT:
    LNRS  d3197616-4b60-4240-9c7f-b9f76a2a3773   Kenney Dam (psc 1)
  model these first, DS-first: LFRA, HARR, FRCN, SETN, BBAR, DOGC, MFRA, TWAC, NARC, COTR, TABR, LCHL, NECR, CHES, LNRS

Fix — pick one:
  1. Model the downstream WSGs first:
       for w in LFRA HARR FRCN SETN BBAR DOGC MFRA TWAC NARC COTR TABR LCHL NECR CHES LNRS; do Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R $w <config>; done
  2. Model LEUT now and settle access after they land:
       Rscript data-raw/wsg_recompute_one.R LEUT <config>
  3. Override, if those dams are known passable / remediated / irrelevant.
     Recorded in the run log and surfaced by lnk_log_read():
       LNK_GUARD_DOWNSTREAM_NOTE="..." Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R LEUT <config>

