link computes accessibility by reading ALREADY-PERSISTED downstream barriers.
Running KHOR now would mark segments accessible that are in fact dammed off, and exit 0.

  persist schema : fresh_default
  unmodelled blocking dams downstream of KHOR:
    CLRH  e65dc967-fba2-44e9-9c7e-9565049c0740   Mica Dam (psc 1)
    REVL  65d93eb9-55ae-4b1d-9d1b-7c1480ea50ac   Revelstoke Dam (psc 1)
  model these first, DS-first: LARL, UARL, REVL, CLRH, CANO

Fix — pick one:
  1. Model the downstream WSGs first:
       for w in LARL UARL REVL CLRH CANO; do Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R $w <config>; done
  2. Model KHOR now and settle access after they land:
       Rscript data-raw/wsg_recompute_one.R KHOR <config>
  3. Override, if those dams are known passable / remediated / irrelevant.
     Recorded in the run log and surfaced by lnk_log_read():
       LNK_GUARD_DOWNSTREAM_NOTE="..." Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R KHOR <config>

